  "In a 2026 controlled experiment (30 artifacts, 150 planted errors, 900 review sessions), a top-tier cross-model reviewer was not significantly different in F1 from same-model review in a fresh session (28.6% cross-context vs 27.1% same-model baseline), and the authors explicitly do not claim equivalence.": null,
  "In the same experiment, cross-model and cross-context review found partly different errors (Jaccard 41.2%), the best cross-model condition (GPT-5.4 as reviewer) scored 32.3% F1 without a significant gain over cross-context review, and 14 cross-model sessions failed (five timeouts or crashes, nine unparseable outputs).": null
